[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2546057201","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100475#issuecomment-2546057201","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100475","id":2546057201,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Xwb_x","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-16T16:16:45Z","updated_at":"2024-12-16T16:18:16Z","body":"Could you alternatively just add another function for the `direction` version, and call it from the old function using a wrapper?\r\n\r\ni.e. Am wondering if there would there be so many of the old cases (even after converting) that it is better to retain the old API as an alternative, to prevent boiler plate in client code.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2546057201/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2546089772","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100475#issuecomment-2546089772","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100475","id":2546089772,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Xwj8s","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-16T16:30:25Z","updated_at":"2024-12-16T16:39:21Z","body":"There are not that many places that call BVH raycast. You can actually see them in the diff :\r\n- `Node3DEditor::gizmo_bvh_ray_query()`\r\n- `GodotSoftBody3D::query_ray()`\r\n- `RendererSceneCull::instances_cull_ray()`\r\n\r\nThe thing is these 3 functions take themselves ray starts and ray ends as parameters.\r\nAnd when you pull the thread you realize that there is a whole stack of other functions behind that pass those ray starts and ends through. It's even exposed this way to GDScript (we might not want to push the change that far for now though, as it would be a breaking change).\r\n\r\nSo I'm not sure wrapping the old logic right in `BVH` would help. But maybe wrapping it at a higher level in the aforementioned PRs may be relevant indeed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2546089772/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2550907101","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100475#issuecomment-2550907101","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100475","id":2550907101,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YC8Dd","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-18T10:07:29Z","updated_at":"2024-12-18T10:07:29Z","body":"Also as usual with these things, do we have any issues where this is causing a problem in practice?\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/contributing/development/best_practices_for_engine_contributors.html\r\n\r\nIf 99% of cases involve a start and end point anyway, whether this calculation is done within the function or externally, it still gets done. And APIs are primarily designed for common use.\r\n\r\nThis is why I was wondering whether it would be better just making the existing function a wrapper, then adding a more accurate version with direction called from this wrapper _if use cases / issues warrant it_.\r\n\r\nThe other question is whether there are precision issues at these large ranges anyway within the ray cast routine. Remember also that Godot can be compiled with `real` as `doubles` which might be another way of addressing same problem.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2550907101/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551039736","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100475#issuecomment-2551039736","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100475","id":2551039736,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YDcb4","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-18T11:11:04Z","updated_at":"2025-07-19T19:29:02Z","body":"Now I understand better your previous comment.\r\n\r\nFor context I'm working on uncapping camera's zfar in the editor (#100896), after having uncapped it in game already (#99986). This would untap the potential of reverse-z in both single and double precision builds.\r\n\r\nFrom the engine's perspective, it's a matter of rewriting in a more precision-friendly way a targeted collection of operations across the rendering and physic logic. This PR is one of them.\r\n\r\nTo your points more specifically : \r\n- **Use case** : large worlds / space games, regular scenes with very large distant objects, and all use cases that wants to use real units for big objects \r\n- **Current usage** : all usages of `ray_query()` I've seen so far _[Edit except 2]_ build the ray endpoint from a normal and a distance (you have sometimes to go back a few wrapping calls to realize it). Taking the latters directly seems to simplify things a little bit\r\n- **Other raycast issues with large numbers** : I haven't identified any other yet. I extensively tested object picking with my local zfar-uncapped editor and it seems to work well with this PR (#100478 on top allows correct interactions with far away guizmos)\r\n\r\nAnyway your questioning is very valid. I think I will make my zfar-uncapped editor PR out first so people can grasp what it brings, and continue the discussion.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551039736/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551123277","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100475#issuecomment-2551123277","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100475","id":2551123277,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YDw1N","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-18T11:51:06Z","updated_at":"2024-12-18T11:51:20Z","body":"Ah and just to make this clear : \n> just making the existing function a wrapper, then adding a more accurate version with direction called from this wrapper\n\nThe precision friendly version requires a ray normal at first hand. This is to avoid `Vector3 ray = (to - start).normalized()` in the current implementation.\n\nSo there is no real point to just call the new one from the old as we would have to do this normalization in the wrapper then.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551123277/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551169342","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100475#issuecomment-2551169342","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100475","id":2551169342,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YD8E-","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-18T12:14:59Z","updated_at":"2024-12-18T12:14:59Z","body":"> The precision friendly version requires a ray normal at first hand. This is to avoid Vector3 ray = (to - start).normalized() in the current implementation.\r\n\r\nYup I understand this - I'm trying to say that if the client code is based around a start and end point (rather than a direction), then this calculation is done somewhere regardless.\r\n\r\nWhether it is done in the client code or in a wrapper function is a matter of convenience for the user, and reduction of boiler plate.\r\n\r\nThere's no precision gain in using this client side:\r\n```\r\n\tVector3 segment = p_ray_end - p_ray_start;\r\n\treal_t length = segment.length();\r\n\tgizmo_bvh.ray_query(p_ray_start, segment / length, length, result);\r\n```\r\nversus doing it in a wrapper, no?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551169342/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551285543","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100475#issuecomment-2551285543","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100475","id":2551285543,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YEYcn","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-18T13:10:29Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T11:55:40Z","body":"Got you. Correct.\r\n\r\nFor now I've seen ~nowhere~ _[edit : twice]_ in the codebase some client code involving start and end positions in the first place. It's all the time the opposite : there is a ray direction and a known far boundary, and the client builds the end position out of it to do the raycast.\r\n\r\nWill share here whenever I stumble upon such a case.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2551285543/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2554132883","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100475#issuecomment-2554132883","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100475","id":2554132883,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YPPmT","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-19T13:57:02Z","updated_at":"2024-12-21T21:06:34Z","body":"Interestingly [Unity](https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.0/Documentation/ScriptReference/Physics.Raycast.html) raycasts with `from`, `direction` and `distance` whereas [Unreal](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/en-us/unreal-engine/using-a-single-line-trace-raycast-by-channel-in-unreal-engine) uses `start` and `end`.\r\n\r\nI found only ~1~ 2 raycasting cases where client code has the ray end position in the first place :\r\n- when `VehicleBody3D` checks for [collisions with the wheels](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/108fd525071f218d424c5d3e2aa9ea151356eeb7/scene/3d/physics/vehicle_body_3d.cpp#L410-L426)\r\n- navigation as it involves starting and ending points by design\r\n\r\nIn both cases though, it's hard to figure out any usage at very large scales, so we can keep using the non-precision proof version there.\r\n\r\nWill keep updating this list :point_up: whenever I find any other case.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2554132883/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5233430159","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100475#issuecomment-5233430159","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100475","id":5233430159,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN-_Ojw","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-09T19:23:45Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T19:23:45Z","body":"Rebased","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5233430159/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]